\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Reacher controller comparison on 500 test rollouts (seeds 10001--10500) per configuration, with $T_{\mathrm  {sim}}=300$. Atlas-DeePC uses $p=8$, with $K=64$ and $d=53$ without guidance, and $K=96$ and $d=57$ with guidance. Select and Contextual denote Select-DPC and Contextual-DPC, respectively. Contextual-DPC uses the same fixed terminal references as unguided Atlas-DeePC. Error statistics summarize final-100 mean fingertip errors across rollouts; timings pool steps 6--300 and were measured in separate sessions. Select timings include all five refinements. Right: success rate versus median online computation time on a logarithmic horizontal axis; Atlas denotes Atlas-DeePC without planning.\relax }}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
